{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A river:</b> The sense, if their waters were dammed — the river of Jerusalem, which was the Gihon." "<b>Her streams:</b> all who dwell in the city of Elohim, which is holy [—] the dwelling of the Most High."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "Reading יחמרו as from חמר ('to dam/muddy'); the syntax of the gloss is compressed and the subject of 'their waters' is left unstated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:59.930533253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}